  "aboutParagraphs": [
    "Tom McCutcheon Disc Golf Park is Lewisville's open, friendly course at Lake Park — redesigned by Dynamic Discs Carrollton and known for holes that require long, accurate shots without ever feeling punishing. From the standard tees it plays 5,324 feet at par 55.",
    "Free to play with concrete tees and Mach 2 baskets, it's the kind of park course where you can air out a midrange and still walk away smiling. The open fairways make it a great place to practice your distance control.",
    "A welcoming DFW staple that's been around since 1998 and keeps improving."
  ],
